From 17b6b288effce935bc11ecd83cc997494f9cd424 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nova <361320585+q2-nova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:38:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] ASoC: cs43130: support shared reset and multi-codec PCM
 routing

Opt in to reference-counted shared reset through cirrus,shared-reset,
including the reset-controller GPIO fallback. Preserve the historical
logical GPIO polarity for existing users. Balance failed resume paths.

Expose PCM channel selection through set_channel_map, retaining the
CS43131 channel-swap sequence. Track clock acquisition per DAI: ALSA
hw_free can follow rejected parameters or run more than once. Validate
formats before acquiring clocks and propagate clock/readiness errors.

Four Q2 codec endpoints pass runtime suspend/reset, cache restoration,
mixer controls and stereo PCM playback tests under QEMU. Physical analog
operation and other codec variants/mixed DSD modes are not qualified.
