 .../devicetree/bindings/sound/cs43130.txt     |   8 +
 sound/soc/codecs/cs43130.c                    | 224 ++++++++++++------
 sound/soc/codecs/cs43130.h                    |   3 +
 3 files changed, 164 insertions(+), 71 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs43130.txt b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs43130.txt
index 8b1dd5aeb..00a29d88f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs43130.txt
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cs43130.txt
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@ Optional properties:
 
   - reset-gpios : Active low GPIO used to reset the device
 
+  - cirrus,shared-reset:
+   Boolean. Reset is shared with other devices. Use the reset-controller
+   framework to reference-count assert/deassert, including its reset-gpios
+   fallback. With this property, reset-gpios polarity describes logical
+   assertion (GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW for a direct connection to the IC's RESET pin).
+   Without it, the historical driver interprets logical GPIO 1 as release.
+   CONFIG_RESET_GPIO is required when using the GPIO fallback.
+
   - cirrus,xtal-ibias:
    When external MCLK is generated by external crystal
    oscillator, CS43130 can be used to provide bias current
